WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.208 --> 00:00:32.833
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna said</b>

2
00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:35.541
<b>that no action binds Him,</b>

3
00:00:35.541 --> 00:00:39.291
<b>nor does He have any desire </b>
<b>for the fruits of action.</b>

4
00:00:39.291 --> 00:00:44.750
<b>He also said that whoever understands</b>
<b>this truth about Him</b>

5
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:48.791
<b>is also not bound by the fruits of their actions.</b>

6
00:00:48.791 --> 00:00:49.500
<b>Now</b>

7
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.666
<b>in this verse, Lord Krishna is referring </b>
<b>to those very sages/ascetics </b>

8
00:00:53.666 --> 00:00:56.125
<b>who understood this truth.</b>

9
00:00:56.125 --> 00:01:01.916
<b>He is encouraging Arjuna to </b>
<b>also follow the same path.</b>

10
00:01:06.583 --> 00:01:09.125
<b>In this verse, Lord Krishna says –</b>

11
00:01:09.125 --> 00:01:14.000
<b>In the past, there have been many such </b>
<b>humans who desired this very liberation.</b>

12
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.291
<b>They too, understanding this knowledge </b>
<b>of renouncing the desire for the fruit,</b>

13
00:01:17.291 --> 00:01:19.416
<b>have been performing their actions.</b>

14
00:01:19.416 --> 00:01:20.625
<b>And Arjuna,</b>

15
00:01:20.625 --> 00:01:26.208
<b>you too should follow them and fulfill your duties.</b>

16
00:01:26.208 --> 00:01:27.041
<b>Here,</b>

17
00:01:27.041 --> 00:01:31.500
<b>Lord Krishna is referring to those sages/ascetics/kings/emperors</b>

18
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.000
<b>who fulfilled all their duties, performed actions,</b>

19
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.583
<b>but by renouncing the desire for the fruit.</b>

20
00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:39.916
<b>Because those people had come to know</b>

21
00:01:39.916 --> 00:01:44.166
<b>that Lord Krishna has no expectation </b>
<b>of the fruit of any action</b>

22
00:01:44.166 --> 00:01:47.708
<b>and He is completely free from </b>
<b>the bondage of action.</b>

23
00:01:47.708 --> 00:01:50.083
<b>By acting with this perspective,</b>

24
00:01:50.083 --> 00:01:53.500
<b>those sages also became free from </b>
<b>the bondage of action.</b>

25
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:59.000
<b>Now here, Lord Krishna is telling </b>
<b>Arjuna to follow them.</b>

26
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.375
<b>Understand this like a treatment</b>
<b>suggested by a doctor.</b>

27
00:02:04.375 --> 00:02:10.375
<b>If in the past, many patients' diseases </b>
<b>have been cured by a particular medicine,</b>

28
00:02:10.375 --> 00:02:14.875
<b>and now that doctor tells you to </b>
<b>take this medicine too,</b>

29
00:02:14.875 --> 00:02:20.583
<b>then it is wise to take such a </b>
<b>medicine without any doubt.</b>

30
00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:27.166
<b>Karma yoga is such a process that has </b>
<b>proven effective for countless people in history,</b>

31
00:02:27.166 --> 00:02:31.416
<b>so now it is appropriate that </b>
<b>Arjuna should also benefit from it.</b>

32
00:02:31.416 --> 00:02:34.791
<b>There was an earlier reference</b>
<b>related to this as well,</b>

33
00:02:34.791 --> 00:02:38.041
<b>where in the thirtieth verse of the third chapter,</b>

34
00:02:38.041 --> 00:02:39.375
<b>Lord Krishna said,</b>

35
00:02:39.375 --> 00:02:40.291
<b>Arjuna,</b>

36
00:02:40.291 --> 00:02:43.250
<b>consider this war as selfless action</b>

37
00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:48.458
<b>and dedicate all its results </b>
<b>to me with full devotion.</b>

38
00:02:48.458 --> 00:02:53.666
<b>That is, if Arjuna fights this war, it should </b>
<b>not be for personal gain or fame,</b>

39
00:02:53.666 --> 00:02:57.333
<b>but only with a sense of duty and dedication.</b>

40
00:02:57.333 --> 00:03:00.833
<b>This will free him from the bondage of action.</b>

41
00:03:00.833 --> 00:03:02.333
<b>Some people think</b>

42
00:03:02.333 --> 00:03:04.375
<b>that the only way to be free from the </b>
<b>bondage of action</b>

43
00:03:04.375 --> 00:03:10.250
<b>is to renounce all actions and live </b>
<b>the life of an ascetic.</b>

44
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:10.916
<b>But</b>

45
00:03:10.916 --> 00:03:14.208
<b>here Krishna is refuting this very misconception.</b>

46
00:03:14.208 --> 00:03:16.375
<b>To be free from the bondage of action,</b>

47
00:03:16.375 --> 00:03:18.458
<b>it is not necessary to renounce action;</b>

48
00:03:18.458 --> 00:03:23.416
<b>what is necessary is to perform that </b>
<b>action selflessly and with devotion.</b>

49
00:03:23.416 --> 00:03:25.750
<b>While fulfilling our duties,</b>

50
00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:27.500
<b>by renouncing the desire for the fruit</b>

51
00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:30.250
<b>and keeping our mind focused on Krishna,</b>

52
00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:33.958
<b>we too can purify our hearts and minds.</b>

53
00:03:33.958 --> 00:03:40.625
<b>The path of acting without attachment leads us</b>
<b>towards spiritual development and liberation.</b>

54
00:03:40.625 --> 00:03:42.625
<b>By following this process,</b>

55
00:03:42.625 --> 00:03:44.375
<b>not only Arjuna,</b>

56
00:03:44.375 --> 00:03:45.291
<b>but</b>

57
00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:50.416
<b>all of us can attain true freedom and satisfaction.</b>

58
00:03:55.333 --> 00:03:56.750
<b>In this verse,</b>

59
00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:00.750
<b>I am advising Arjuna, and you as well,</b>

60
00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:06.458
<b>to take inspiration from those</b>
<b>great sages and devotees</b>

61
00:04:06.458 --> 00:04:13.166
<b>who attained liberation by following </b>
<b>this very path of selfless action.</b>

62
00:04:13.166 --> 00:04:18.625
<b>All these scholars understood </b>
<b>the divine nature of their actions</b>

63
00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:24.291
<b>and fulfilled their duties without </b>
<b>attachment to the result.</b>

64
00:04:24.291 --> 00:04:25.708
<b>Just understand it like this,</b>

65
00:04:25.708 --> 00:04:31.375
<b>that I, like a physician, am telling you </b>
<b>to take a medicine</b>

66
00:04:31.375 --> 00:04:38.125
<b>that has freed many patients like you who</b>
<b>were trapped in the bondage of karma.</b>

67
00:04:38.125 --> 00:04:44.333
<b>This perspective inspires you to perform </b>
<b>all your responsibilities with the feeling</b>

68
00:04:44.333 --> 00:04:47.458
<b>that your every action is dedicated </b>
<b>not for personal gain,</b>

69
00:04:47.458 --> 00:04:48.166
<b>but</b>

70
00:04:48.166 --> 00:04:53.625
<b>only to a higher purpose of devotion </b>
<b>and human welfare.</b>

71
00:04:53.625 --> 00:04:55.541
<b>For example,</b>

72
00:04:55.541 --> 00:04:58.708
<b>when you cook a meal for your family,</b>

73
00:04:58.708 --> 00:05:00.916
<b>you are doing it not for any praise,</b>

74
00:05:00.916 --> 00:05:01.708
<b>but</b>

75
00:05:01.708 --> 00:05:05.500
<b>for the health of your family members, </b>
<b>for their happiness,</b>

76
00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:10.166
<b>for a smile of satisfaction on their faces.</b>

77
00:05:10.166 --> 00:05:15.916
<b>Just by making a small change in perspective,</b>

78
00:05:15.916 --> 00:05:21.125
<b>a daily action becomes so liberating, so sublime.</b>

79
00:05:21.125 --> 00:05:25.875
<b>You can adopt this same attitude </b>
<b>whenever you perform any action.</b>

80
00:05:25.875 --> 00:05:27.041
<b>Remember,</b>

81
00:05:27.041 --> 00:05:28.875
<b>this path of doing your work selflessly,</b>

82
00:05:28.875 --> 00:05:33.500
<b>with a sense of service and devotion,</b>

83
00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:36.375
<b>has led many to liberation.</b>

84
00:05:36.375 --> 00:05:41.208
<b>And yes, also know that renouncing attachment</b>

85
00:05:41.208 --> 00:05:43.750
<b>does not mean renouncing your interest in work,</b>

86
00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:49.750
<b>but doing your work with full dedication and joy.</b>

87
00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:57.333
<b>The only difference is that you </b>
<b>are dedicating it to someone else.</b>

88
00:05:57.333 --> 00:06:00.625
<b>Just try bringing this thought to your mind,</b>

89
00:06:00.625 --> 00:06:04.583
<b>that I am doing this work with full dedication,</b>

90
00:06:04.583 --> 00:06:08.125
<b>so that a smile comes on someone else's face.</b>

91
00:06:08.125 --> 00:06:10.916
<b>This very thought will delight you.</b>

92
00:06:10.916 --> 00:06:14.875
<b>This perspective not only ultimately</b>
<b>leads to liberation</b>

93
00:06:14.875 --> 00:06:15.791
<b>but</b>

94
00:06:15.791 --> 00:06:20.583
<b>also reduces the stress and anxiety of daily life.</b>

95
00:06:20.583 --> 00:06:21.750
<b>Think about it.</b>

96
00:06:26.458 --> 00:06:37.166
<b>Just as many great sages performed their duties </b>
<b>without attachment, only with spiritual goals,</b>

97
00:06:37.166 --> 00:06:38.833
<b>learning from that,</b>

98
00:06:38.833 --> 00:06:43.666
<b>you too can apply these principles </b>
<b>in the family environment.</b>

99
00:06:43.666 --> 00:06:46.000
<b>You too can renounce personal interest</b>

100
00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:51.666
<b>and do every action only with the spiritual </b>
<b>feeling of love and welfare.</b>

101
00:06:51.666 --> 00:06:55.208
<b>In a family, there are many people</b>
<b>and many responsibilities,</b>

102
00:06:55.208 --> 00:06:57.500
<b>whether it is raising children,</b>

103
00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:00.583
<b>assisting someone in household chores,</b>

104
00:07:00.583 --> 00:07:04.583
<b>helping each other in life goals, etc.</b>

105
00:07:04.583 --> 00:07:09.875
<b>If these responsibilities are fulfilled with </b>
<b>a sense of service without attachment,</b>

106
00:07:09.875 --> 00:07:14.291
<b>family relationships will become even stronger.</b>

107
00:07:14.291 --> 00:07:15.666
<b>But</b>

108
00:07:15.666 --> 00:07:19.583
<b>a doubt must have certainly arisen in the mind,</b>

109
00:07:19.583 --> 00:07:24.750
<b>that renouncing attachment </b>
<b>in the family environment</b>

110
00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:28.916
<b>seems like giving up caring for family members.</b>

111
00:07:28.916 --> 00:07:30.125
<b>No,</b>

112
00:07:30.125 --> 00:07:32.250
<b>it is not like that at all.</b>

113
00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:34.083
<b>Understand this point.</b>

114
00:07:34.083 --> 00:07:38.583
<b>Renouncing attachment in the</b>
<b>family environment only means</b>

115
00:07:38.583 --> 00:07:45.916
<b>that you focus your attention on duties, </b>
<b>focus on the well-being of family members,</b>

116
00:07:45.916 --> 00:07:48.291
<b>not on the result.</b>

117
00:07:48.291 --> 00:07:51.750
<b>Real care is to help, right? =</b>

118
00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:58.791
<b>The result is just a conclusion of actions </b>
<b>and help received from others.</b>

119
00:07:58.791 --> 00:08:00.458
<b>For example,</b>

120
00:08:00.458 --> 00:08:04.583
<b>parents provide the highest </b>
<b>education to their children,</b>

121
00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:07.833
<b>guide them in their personal development,</b>

122
00:08:07.833 --> 00:08:08.583
<b>but</b>

123
00:08:08.583 --> 00:08:16.958
<b>at the same time also know that your </b>
<b>children have to make their own life experiences.</b>

124
00:08:16.958 --> 00:08:24.125
<b>Just as every good and bad result taught you </b>
<b>something in your adolescence,</b>

125
00:08:24.125 --> 00:08:25.291
<b>in the same way,</b>

126
00:08:25.291 --> 00:08:29.416
<b>your children will also learn from their results,</b>

127
00:08:29.416 --> 00:08:33.208
<b>this is what will shape their character.</b>

128
00:08:33.208 --> 00:08:37.416
<b>As parents, you are helpers, well-wishers,</b>

129
00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:38.333
<b>but</b>

130
00:08:38.333 --> 00:08:42.625
<b>this path is ultimately your child's.</b>

131
00:08:42.625 --> 00:08:44.083
<b>Not only for children,</b>

132
00:08:44.083 --> 00:08:51.041
<b>but when you help other family members </b>
<b>and relatives without selfishness,</b>

133
00:08:51.041 --> 00:08:55.000
<b>it will sweeten the mutual relationships.</b>

134
00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.333
<b>Also,</b>

135
00:08:56.333 --> 00:09:00.666
<b>when you do your personal </b>
<b>actions with concentration,</b>

136
00:09:00.666 --> 00:09:04.666
<b>without being influenced by good or bad results,</b>

137
00:09:04.666 --> 00:09:08.500
<b>it also becomes a lesson for others in the family.</b>

138
00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:11.416
<b>This is also the welfare of others,</b>

139
00:09:11.416 --> 00:09:15.000
<b>this is also spiritual thinking.</b>

140
00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.375
<b>Think about it.</b>

141
00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:25.125
<b>In professional life, it is necessary</b>

142
00:09:25.125 --> 00:09:30.958
<b>that you do your work with complete </b>
<b>dedication and enthusiasm,</b>

143
00:09:30.958 --> 00:09:32.625
<b>but</b>

144
00:09:32.625 --> 00:09:35.583
<b>without being attached to the results.</b>

145
00:09:35.583 --> 00:09:42.625
<b>Just as I am inspiring Arjuna to </b>
<b>follow the ancient sages,</b>

146
00:09:42.625 --> 00:09:44.000
<b>in the same way,</b>

147
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.208
<b>you too</b>

148
00:09:45.208 --> 00:09:51.291
<b>can take inspiration from those </b>
<b>mentors in your professional field </b>

149
00:09:51.291 --> 00:09:58.375
<b>who have fulfilled their responsibilities </b>
<b>with ethics and dedication.</b>

150
00:09:58.375 --> 00:10:00.083
<b>Think,</b>

151
00:10:00.083 --> 00:10:05.875
<b>who are those people whose names </b>
<b>everyone takes with great respect.</b>

152
00:10:05.875 --> 00:10:09.375
<b>Someone who brought about</b>
<b>a big change in society,</b>

153
00:10:09.375 --> 00:10:14.791
<b>someone made a great invention, </b>
<b>someone is respected in the field of art.</b>

154
00:10:14.791 --> 00:10:19.250
<b>When you read about their lives, you will know</b>

155
00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:26.000
<b>that in most circumstances their</b>
<b>focus was only on their actions,</b>

156
00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:29.458
<b>focused on contributing to society.</b>

157
00:10:29.458 --> 00:10:33.291
<b>Their focus was not on success or wealth.</b>

158
00:10:33.291 --> 00:10:37.166
<b>Their purpose was only to do excellent work.</b>

159
00:10:37.166 --> 00:10:38.541
<b>Just understand it like this,</b>

160
00:10:38.541 --> 00:10:42.791
<b>that success was not even the </b>
<b>destination of their path,</b>

161
00:10:42.791 --> 00:10:47.041
<b>they just kept walking on the path of </b>
<b>hard work and dedication,</b>

162
00:10:47.041 --> 00:10:53.333
<b>and success was just a milestone </b>
<b>that came on its own.</b>

163
00:10:53.333 --> 00:10:54.625
<b>Also,</b>

164
00:10:54.625 --> 00:10:58.000
<b>when you work with this perspective,</b>

165
00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:03.625
<b>it also becomes a source of</b>
<b>inspiration for your colleagues,</b>

166
00:11:03.625 --> 00:11:08.291
<b>that they too should focus only on their hard work,</b>

167
00:11:08.291 --> 00:11:10.708
<b>success will come automatically.</b>

168
00:11:10.708 --> 00:11:12.000
<b>Think,</b>

169
00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:19.833
<b>in a way, you too become like those</b>
<b>people who inspired you.</b>

170
00:11:19.833 --> 00:11:22.500
<b>Inspiring someone towards goodness,</b>

171
00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:25.833
<b>this is also human welfare.</b>

172
00:11:25.833 --> 00:11:28.791
<b>This is also spiritual thinking.</b>

173
00:11:28.791 --> 00:11:33.250
<b>And if gradually such people keep increasing,</b>

174
00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:41.250
<b>imagine how positive and effective the </b>
<b>environment of your workplace will become.</b>

175
00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:42.916
<b>Imagine it</b>

176
00:11:42.916 --> 00:11:46.000
<b>and understand the hints.</b>

